@startuml join-handshake
' Revision 2026-10-12: F-7 replay relies on durable effect claims/admission floors; wire formats remain pending.
title Join handshake (revision 4): a server challenge, a signed canonical transcript, atomic invitation consumption; anchors: the Web PKI, DNSSEC validated in the client (default), and the invitation's pins (fallback for an environment without a DNSSEC domain)

participant "Human-run init / donor bridge role\n(A/C: donor UID; B: bridge UID)" as C
database "DNS: system resolver,\nDNS-over-HTTPS as the fallback\n(signatures validated inside the client)" as R
participant "Join point\n(our host)" as JP
actor "Operator" as OP
participant "Registry / key keeper" as T
participant "swarma-dispatcher (service UID)\nroot swarma-user-manager helper\nproject workplace provisioning" as D

note over C, T
  Anchors before first contact:
  (a) the Web PKI certificate of the join point's domain;
  (b) default: DNSSEC-secure TXT _swarma.<domain> = root fingerprint, TXT _swarma-ssh-ca.<domain> = our SSH host CA key, TLSA = the join point's TLS key, validated inside the client from the embedded root trust anchor (a closed network brings its own zone trust anchor);
  (c) the invitation (marketplace deal thread, e-mail, our site) with the same fingerprints and a one-use random code (>= 128 bits): the fallback when the environment has no DNSSEC domain, a cross-check otherwise.
  Proof of possession: the transcript signed over a SERVER challenge (not a client nonce).
  No human second channel and nothing for the donor to configure. No step downgrades on failure.
end note

alt invitation declares no DNSSEC domain (chosen before lookup)
  C -> C: use invitation root/host-CA/TLS pins; Web PKI required
else default DNSSEC (open application requires this branch)
  C -> R: TXT _swarma, TXT _swarma-ssh-ca, TLSA (per environment, not worker)
  R --> C: records (client validates signatures, not resolver AD bit)
  C -> C: indeterminate/system DNS missing signatures: retry transport over DoH
  break mismatch, bogus, failed/malformed read or still indeterminate
    C -> C: refuse; DNS failure never selects invitation fallback
  end
  C -> C: secure; must agree with invitation pins when present
end
C -> JP: POST /join/challenge (invited/open enrolment reference; schema pending)\nHTTPS: Web PKI + selected trust pins
JP -> JP: bound to this enrolment, fresh, within attempt/queue limits?
JP --> C: server_challenge (5 min)
C -> C: transcript = canonical CBOR, domain-separated:\n{version, invitation reference when invited, project, role, variant, K_sig, K_enc, K_ssh, server_challenge, client_nonce, expires_at, algorithms}
C -> JP: HTTPS: Web PKI for the domain, selected DNSSEC/TLSA or declared invitation pins
C -> JP: POST /join/cert {transcript, sig_K_sig(transcript), code only when invited}
alt invited
  JP -> JP: constant-time code check; signature/challenge/expiry; atomic consumption;\ntombstone; same-key retry -> same enrolment, other key -> refuse
else open application (no code)
  JP -> JP: signature/challenge/expiry; operator queue; exact binding/retry schema pending
end
JP -> JP: per-address/per-invitation/queue limits
break invalid signature/challenge/expiry, wrong-key retry, invitation limits or full queue
  JP --> C: refuse; no package
end
JP -> OP: show {enrolment reference (schema pending), fingerprint, name, role}
OP -> OP: check against the donor's signed marketplace card when there is one,\notherwise invitation binding or open application; no voice check
break operator rejects application
  OP -> JP: reject
  JP --> C: refused
end
OP -> T: pin K_sig, K_enc, K_ssh; root-signed admission; grants (scope, expiry)
OP -> D: provision project workplace; issue short user certificate for its principal\n(project-side account boundary; separate from donor provisioner)
OP -> OP: package with host CA + short user certificate/principal, variant/tuple and binding; no carrier credential; AEAD to K_enc with AAD = H(transcript); signed by the operator certificate (root-signed, scope onboard)
OP -> JP: release package for this enrolment (reference schema pending)
C -> JP: POST /join/challenge (collection phase, second challenge; pending schema)
C -> JP: POST /join/collect {enrolment reference, sig_K_sig(second challenge)}
JP --> C: package
C -> C: decrypt with K_enc; verify operator cert chain to the pinned root;\nverify package signature; check AAD; pin our SSH host CA key from the package\nAND cross-check it against DNS (or the invitation)

break invalid package chain/signature/AAD or host-CA mismatch
  C -> C: refuse package activation; no trust fallback
end

note over C, T
  All invitation/transcript/package and join API/error schemas PENDING (protocol/remote-worker.md).
  Open-domain application has no code; exact identifiers/retry binding pending; operator admission required.
  Pinned afterwards:
  on our side K_sig, K_enc, K_ssh in the registry; K_ssh reaches the workplace user only through short certificates of our user CA (TrustedUserCAKeys);
  on the donor side our root, the operator certificate, our SSH host CA key (@cert-authority), the binding digest, the qualified tuple, the policy generation.
  Every later message: signed over exact bytes by K_sig on the donor, fresh, replay-checked, grant-checked (ADM).
  Replay: invited cert meets its tombstone; collection proof/retry format pending; later frame effects rely on durable binding-generation-scoped operation-identity/canonical-argument-digest claims with authenticated admission floors (CIP-0009 D5); connection IDs and the output cache do not authorize retry mutation.
  Rotation: a new host key gets a new host certificate (no DNS change); a host CA rotation publishes the new key beside the old; operator cert -> root-signed record; K -> operator revocation, user KRL, close sessions + new enrolment.
  Certificates: host about one year, user about one day (policy examples); bridge renews user certificate.
  Key storage/algorithm admission follows D0; B disabled until separate provisioner contract exists.
end note
note over C, T
  Phase: Draft donor target, A first after slice 0; B disabled pending separate provisioner.
  Curator init: human donor UID; bridge role: A/C donor UID or future B bridge UID.
  Join point and registry/keeper service UIDs unspecified in spec CIP-0009 D4/D9/D12.
  Join point owns challenges, queue, atomic invitation tombstones and stored packages;
  registry/keeper owns public key pins/admission/grants and CA authority;
  donor bridge owns private keys and protected package/config/CA trust state.
  Host root owns sshd CA/KRL policy; workplace UID never controls SSH authorization.
  Invalid/replayed/wrong-key proof, expired challenge/invitation or queue cap -> refuse.
  Same-key invited retry recovers same pending enrollment; collection retry format pending.
  [[../CIP-0009-donor-side-deployment-and-bridge.md#recommendation CIP-0009 D4/D6/D9/D12]]
  [[../../protocol/remote-worker.md#trust-and-ssh Selected trust and CAs]]
end note

@enduml
